  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\vec{a}=\\hat{i}+\\hat{j}+\\hat{k}, \\vec{b}=2 \\hat{i}+4 \\hat{j}-5 \\hat{k}$ and $\\vec{c}=x \\hat{i}+2 \\hat{j}+3 \\hat{k}, x \\in \\mathbb{R}$.\nIf $\\vec{d}$ is the unit vector in the direction of $\\vec{b}+\\vec{c}$ such that $\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{d}=1$, then $(\\vec{a} \\times \\vec{b}) \\cdot \\vec{c}$ is equal to",
